---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const pillars = [
  { name: 'Health', means: 'Physical strength, metabolic health, longevity.', framework: 'The Long Strongs — the Long Strong Ladder' },
  { name: 'Finance', means: 'Financial peace, debt freedom, building wealth.', framework: 'Dave Ramsey — the Baby Steps' },
  { name: 'Community', means: 'Being a good parent, spouse, child, sibling, friend, and community member.', framework: 'In progress' },
  { name: 'Motivator', means: 'Finding joy — purpose, passion, what gets you out of bed.', framework: 'In progress' },
  { name: 'Time', means: "Protecting what matters, eliminating what doesn't.", framework: 'In progress' },
];
---
<Base title="Longevity Pillars — Miranda Essig" description="To philosophize on what makes for a fulfilled life and how to get there.">
  <section style="background-color:#6f7d57" class="text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16">
      <p class="uppercase tracking-widest text-white/80 text-sm">Longevity Pillars</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold max-w-3xl">Longevity Fuel</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-white/90 max-w-2xl">To philosophize on what makes for a fulfilled life and how to get there.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">When we are born, a deck of cards is shuffled: the body we inhabit, the family we inherit, the community around us. That is our starting hand. From there we can improve it slowly over time, stick with what we got, or self-sabotage.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Health is only one pillar of a bigger life. These five are the philosophy underneath everything else on this site.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
    {pillars.map((p) => (
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6">
        <span class="block w-10 h-1.5 rounded mb-4" style="background-color:#6f7d57"></span>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">{p.name}</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mt-2 leading-relaxed">{p.means}</p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-3 text-ink"><span class="text-muted">Framework:</span> {p.framework}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Choose your hard</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Every pillar has a version of pain. Pain now is the growth path — the harder choice that pays off later. Pain later is the easier choice that costs you more in the end. You don't get to avoid pain; you only get to choose which kind.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Pain now · growth</h3>
        <p class="text-muted mt-1">Real food, movement, a budget, showing up for people.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Pain later · fixed</h3>
        <p class="text-muted mt-1">Fake food, the couch, minimum payments, looking away.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">The goal isn't to work on all five at once. Go intense on the one that needs you most, cruise in the others until it's ingrained — then shift. And be different, but let others choose their hard.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
